laurel 2906: wired memory guard for IOSurfaces (port of negroni 0399).

bsd/dev/laurel_wired.c: laurel_wired_allow(bytes, what) keeps the system's wired pages (vm_page_wire_count) at
or below 55 % of max_mem (backboardd and SpringBoard exempt). SweetSurface.cpp asks it before a buffer surface
is allocated (one condition next to SWEET_SURFACE_WIRED_MAX); a refusal is kIOReturnNoMemory, so an app gets an
allocation failure instead of the system running out of pageable memory (negroni freeze of 2026-10-27).
Lines: "LAUREL WIRED: on: ..." at the first surface, one "near the limit" per boot, rate-limited "refused".
Kill switch laurelwiredguard=0. The GPU buffer paths (RedwoodGPU / TopazAdreno, GPU area) can call the same
function; they are not hooked here.

Review fixes: M3 backboardd and SpringBoard are exempt; the limit is 55 % of max_mem, i.e. of the 2100 RAM window
(3264 MiB -> 1795 MiB wired; 768 MiB fallback -> 422 MiB), both in the "LAUREL WIRED: on:" line. Rebased after
area A 2101 (the hook stays in the non-pool buffer path, before laurel_surf_pages); area B's 2151 rebases on top.

